    "background_story": "Evie was a brilliant and fearless archaeologist, known for her groundbreaking research on ancient medical practices. Her latest obsession was the mysterious art of trephination, a form of skull surgery performed by ancient civilizations. While on an expedition in Peru, Evie stumbled upon an Inca temple hidden deep in the Andes. As she carefully excavated the site, she discovered a series of ancient skulls, each bearing the telltale signs of trephination. Her team's findings sparked a flurry of interest in the academic community, and Evie became a leading expert on the subject. Her work shed new light on the ingenuity and sophistication of ancient cultures, challenging conventional wisdom about the origins of modern medicine. Evie's fearless pursuit of knowledge and her passion for the past continue to inspire a new generation of archaeologists and medical historians.",
